Z||000010||Bald Dude||11-10-2000||08:19 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 2M4 Dale:<P><B>I , personally, hope that that junky OPEL doesn't make an entry into the states as a Fiero.....Just more bad press......seems like it is poorly constructed.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Dale,  I don't want to rain on your parade,  well maybe I do.  That "junky OPEL" is based on the Lotus Elise.  Sales are through the roof, in all it's variants (Lotus Elise, Opel Speedster and Vauxhaul VX220), The Elise has gotten raves in the European press and I'm glad that at least one American magazine can see the potential.<P>Mark<P><p>[This message has been edited by Bald Dude (edited 11-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||ur2biteme||11-10-2000||08:35 PM||||well, before i start flames, let me start off with this:<P>the fiero has always impressed me as a well put together and thought out vehicle.  maybe not the best in this category, but its much closer to the top than the bottom.  <P>now, with that said, what i saw of the speedster, it is another well put together and thought out car.  i'd have to agree with motor trend and say that when and if another fiero is released, i'll be more than willing to fork out the $30k current pricetag for one, so long as it has all the cushy GT options and a stick, of course   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>UR2BITEME<BR>'87 econo coupe<BR>170k and a bad fender :(||||reg||1
